Practical philosophy

        (1) by a truth of practical logic, absent knowledge of whether ∃ a ground (stable ground)
          and, if so, what it consists in, that knowledge (ground knowledge) is itself
          a ground (the default ground)
            : re `^*\(\d+\) (.+)`s see `^*argue\+ that, ${same}`p @ default/._/text.notes.brec
        (2) despite long efforts [in the past], ultimately|{in the end} {we have}|{∃ among us}
          (at present) no settled consensus on the ground question or its likes
            : re `the ground question` sc. `whether ∃ a ground.+and.+what it consists in`s
        (3) we know|have (at present) of no way|method to [reliably]
          {gauge|determine|predict an upper limit|bound on}|bound
          {how long}|{the period|{length of time}} it could|might take to acquire ground knowledge

        : see `^*\(1\)`
        : see `^*\(2\)`
        : see `^*\(3\)` :
